  "projects": [
   {
    "name": "Knowledge Depot LMS Upgrade",
    "description": "Performed a vendor software upgrade on on-the-shelf software supporting the Knowledge Depot Learning Management System first installed in 2011.  All aspects of the system were upgraded, and due to the challenge of having a live system up until cutover, the new version was built in parallel to support tasks of the existing software.  My role was similar to that of the original installation project, where I would work with vendor and internal teams to spec out hardware and infrastructure.  As we now understood how the vendor's previous version operated under a \"Depot\"​ load, we significantly bumped the architecture.  The vendor's newer version also had several architectural changes such as:\n- Redhat Enterprise 6.x, from 5.x\n- Apache httpd 2.4, from 2.2\n- Tomcat 7.0.x, from JBoss 4.2.2\n- Java 1.7, from Java 1.5.  \n\nWorked with Oracle DBA team, infrastructure team, and vendor again when days after go-live, the \"Depot\" load brought the system down.  Worked side by side with matrix teams to determine optimal settings of the vendor product on our infrastructure.  Drove vendor to upgrade certain libraries that were found to be detrimental in multithreaded environments.  ",
    "is_current": false
   },
   {
    "name": "Knowledge Depot Learning Management System",
    "description": "Replaced existing custom e-Learning tracking system with a new off-the-shelf solution that would provide the business with state-of-the-art e-Learning, self-paced, and instructor-led training for store associates.  \n- Worked with vendor and internal teams to specify hardware size for 350,000 users. \n- Set up environment (RHEL 5.5, httpd 2.2, JBoss 4.2, Java 1.5) in QA, Performance Test, and Production. \n- Implemented single signon to product.  At the time neither vendor not THD had standard SSO architecture.  \n\nSystem stability became a main concern during the first few weeks after go-live.  Worked with vendor to aggressively tune their software for our infrastructure and load. \n- Tuned Hotspot 1.5 JVM parameters \n- Tuned Apache 2.2 and JBoss 4.2 to accept higher number of requests.  \n- Worked with Oracle DBA and vendor on slow queries. \n- Developed documentation for off shore groups to administer environment during off-hours processing and weekly system restarts.  \n- Worked with SAN engineering to migrate Oracle database to faster IO devices as they became available.\n- Worked with Store Network to develop an aggressive caching solution using squid in each store location.  Developed scripts to facilitate a nightly prefetch of content using bash and wget.  ",
    "associated_with": "The Home Depot",
    "is_current": false
   }
